.SH NAME
hsh - A command prompt

.SH SYNOPSIS
hsh : To enter interactive mode
echo [command] | hsh : To execute commands in non-intaractive mode

.SH DESCRIPTION
A simple shell that executes commands and executables from user or scripts input

Input is fetched directly from STDIN, then tokenized and interpreted.

The shell currently supports two builtins:

exit : Exits the shell.
env : Prints the environment variables

It also supports searching through the path to execute other commands

